<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 35 — Security Fundamentals & Threat Modeling.
    identity/     Caller, roles, a small HMAC-signed token (replaced by OAuth 2.1 / JWT in chapters 36-37)
    orders/       object, property and function level authorization (OWASP API1, API3, API5), page limits (API4)
    auth/         password storage (PBKDF2, 600,000 iterations) and login throttling (API2)
    outbound/     server-side request forgery protection for webhooks (API7, API10)
    threatmodel/  STRIDE per element, as code, checked in the build
    web/          the Spring MVC adapter
  The security code has no framework dependencies; verify/run.sh compiles and measures it with a JDK alone.
-->
